Description:
  Standalone Company workspace section page.

  Renders one company section on its own semantic route, as the counterpart to the consolidated
  company workspace. The section label, description and body are resolved by the server from
  CompanySectionRegistry, so this page never names a section itself and never decides which
  sections a reader may see.

  The selected-company control is included directly beneath the heading so a platform
  administrator can change which company is in context without leaving the section.

  WARNING: a template comment is not a safe place to document syntax. F3 parses its own tags
  inside comments, so a tag written out as a usage example becomes a real tag in the compiled
  template. A comment delimiter written inside a comment body ends it early and leaks the
  remainder onto the page. Keep every comment plain prose: no angle brackets, no comment
  delimiters, no template tokens and no code, not even to document one.
Changelog:
  2026/09/07 17:00 SAST
  - The page header sits above the section wrapper rather than inside it. Inside, the wrapper's own top padding pushed the header down the page, which is why only the Company routes showed a band of white space above their heading.
  2026/09/07 15:10 SAST
  - Uses the shared page header rather than a heading block of its own.
  2026/08/29 14:32 SAST
  - Added the required file metadata header and reindented with tabs; the entire file was
